```

## 6. HTML version

```html
<a href="https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/actions/workflows/WORKFLOW_FILE">
  <img src="https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/actions/workflows/WORKFLOW_FILE/badge.svg" alt="ALT TEXT">
</a>
```

## 7. Troubleshooting grey / “no status” badge

Common causes:

- Workflow has never run.
- Workflow is disabled.
- Repo is private and the viewer isn’t authenticated.
- Wrong owner, repo, or workflow filename.
- Workflow file is not on the branch you’re requesting.
- Branch parameter doesn’t match where the workflow exists.
- Actions are disabled for the repo.
- You’re viewing a fork; the badge shows the fork’s status.

## 8. How to find the exact workflow filename

1. Open the repo on GitHub.
2. Go to the **Actions** tab.
3. Click the workflow.
4. Look at the URL — it will contain:
   ```
   /actions/workflows/FILENAME
   ```
5. Or check the repo’s `.github/workflows/` directory.

